133. Pagination
Pagination is the process of splitting a large dataset into smaller, discrete pages.
Instead of loading thousands of rows from a database all at once—which slows down your app and crashes browsers—you request a small chunk (like 10 or 20 rows) at a time.

using LIMIT and OFFSET
Limit/Top : How many rows to show per page.
Offset    : How many rows to skip past before showing the data.
Amazon showing 20 products per page.
Page Size = 5
First Page
SELECT *
FROM employees
LIMIT 5;

Output
emp_id
1
2
3
4
5
Second Page
SELECT *
FROM employees
LIMIT 5 OFFSET 5;

Output
emp_id
6
7
8
9
10


