140. SQL vs ORM
SQL (Structured Query Language) is the standard programming language used to manage, store, and manipulate data within a relational database.
ORM (Object Relational Mapping) allows developers to interact with databases using programming language objects instead of writing SQL manually.

> SELECT *
  FROM employees

> employee = session.query(Employee)

           SQL	                         ORM
Write SQL queries manually	     Uses programming language objects
Faster for complex queries	      Easier for CRUD operations
  More control	                  Less boilerplate code
 Better performance	             Better developer productivity


Real-Time Example
Banking systems often use raw SQL for maximum performance.
Django applications commonly use an ORM for faster development.


141. MySQL vs PostgreSQL
