143. CAP Theorem
CAP Theorem states that a distributed database can guarantee only two out of three properties at the same time.
consistency - Every user sees the same latest data.
availability - Every request receives a response.
partition tolerance - The system continues working even if communication between servers fails.

The Setup: You are texting a friend on WhatsApp.
The Partition (Network Break):- You step into an elevator and completely lose your internet connection.
The Availability:- The app doesn’t freeze or crash. It stays open, lets you type a new message, and saves it locally on your phone with a clock icon 🕒.
The Missing Piece (Consistency):-  Because you are disconnected, your friend cannot see your message yet. Your phone has the message, but the WhatsApp server does not.
The Recovery:-  You step out of the elevator. Your phone reconnects, sends the queued message, and your friend finally sees it.


